A||||5||FIERO1985||NOTHBACK TO FASTBACK CONVERSION>???||||1||
Z||000000||FIERO1985||12-10-2001||12:22 PM||||I am interested in converting my 85gt to a fastback. How is this done? What Kits? Prices? Thanks for any and all feedback.<P>Thanks<BR>Dan<P>------------------<BR>1985 GT V6 <BR>"LETS RACE"||||reg||1
Z||000001||Old Lar||12-10-2001||01:36 PM||||No "kit" needed.  Remove the rear clip from the roof line back from the coupe.  Add fast back clip.  You'll need a fastback deck and deck vents. Maybe some fastback sailpanels.  I'm not sure how the tail light assemblies fit from the coupe to the fastback.<P>You'll need to disassemble the interior to access the bolts that hold the rear clip on.<P>If you are real lucky you could get a fastback clip and deck in the same color.  Contact the Fiero parts vendors on the forum list: like Kick Hill Farms, Ed Parks, Bob Steiger.  They may have all the materials you will need and some helpful hints on how to do it.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Fiero_24||12-10-2001||02:27 PM||||I did a swap and it was not hard.  It is very time consuming though.  I did the whole swap by myself, with just a little help to get the rear clip on.  Here are some pics of mine: <BR> <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fiero_24/fieros.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fiero_24/fieros.html</A> <P><P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/driverside41.jpg"> <BR>  <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fiero_24" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fiero_24</A> <BR>1987 GT||||reg||12
Z||000003||RedGTFieroKCMO||12-10-2001||07:20 PM||||Fiero_24, did you also modify the wiring? Please give me more details on what you did to get all the tail lamps to function. I need to find more sockets for the amber turn signals to finish mine. Thanks!<P>  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Fiero_24:<BR><B>I did a swap and it was not hard.  It is very time consuming though.  I did the whole swap by myself, with just a little help to get the rear clip on.  Here are some pics of mine: <BR> <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fiero_24/fieros.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fiero_24/fieros.html</A> <P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><p>[This message has been edited by RedGTFieroKCMO (edited 12-10-2001).]||||reg||5
Z||000004||Fiero_24||12-10-2001||08:33 PM||||I bought a Gt wiring harness, but there was a short in it.  I used the Ferrari look alike tail lamps, so I did not use the GT wiring harness.  I originally filed down the GT lamp sockets to accept the coupe sockets.  The only down side is that you only have the red and no amber turn signals.  I could not figure out the wiring to make a coupe harness a GT harness.  I wired in the PONTIAC with the side marker lights, but then the PONTIAC only lights up with the parking lamps on.  If you are interested in the tail lamp sockets, I have some.  I cut them all off of the shot GT wiring harness.  I do not know where they are, but I will look for them when I go to WI next weekend to finish adjusting my new V6.  I cannot gaurantee I still have them, I threw a lot of stuff out.  <P>Craig<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/driverside41.jpg"> <BR>  <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fiero_24" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fiero_24</A> <BR>1987 GT||||reg||10
Z||000005||SCCA FIERO||12-10-2001||09:09 PM||||Feel free to check out my website. I did this to my 88 Coupe and documented the process.<P> <A HREF="http://msnhomepages.talkcity.com/RallyRd/scca_fiero/" TARGET=_blank>http://msnhomepages.talkcity.com/RallyRd/scca_fiero/</A> <P>The swap isn't hard if you have all the parts. I think it took me about 7 hours to do mine.||||reg||1
